        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Maple Leafs' offseason isn't about dwelling on a 78-point stumble that ended in 8th place in the Atlantic; it's about surgical reshaping before the cap clock ticks louder. <strong>The club has parted ways with AGM Hayley Wickenheiser</strong>, a move that signals a fresh philosophical direction as the front office recalibrates its scouting and development pipeline. With no playoff ghosts haunting the air, the focus shifts to draft capital and free-agent targets who can fill the defensive gaps exposed last year - think finding the ideal partner for Darren Raddysh, a question now dominating internal debates. Prospect Timofei Obvintsev's new AHL contract adds depth, while Ben Danford's quiet ascent with the Marlies hints at a homegrown solution on the blue line. <strong>What to watch: whether the Leafs aggressively pursue a top-six forward or double down on defensive reinvestment before July 15 free agency opens.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 12, 2026"
      },
