      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Blue Jays are a team that can't quite hold its lead, a flaw that cost them again in San Diego. <strong>Jays fell to Padres 8-7</strong> on Friday, a heartbreaker that extends a one-game losing streak and leaves them at 45-50, sitting fourth in the AL East 12 games behind the division leader. The loss came down to Trey Yesavage, who lacked command in a short outing and couldn't stop the Padres' rally even after Vladimir Guerrero Jr. and the offense had built a lead. Earlier in the series, the Jays showed flashes of life - beating the Padres 5-3 and crushing the Giants 10-0 - but consistency remains the missing piece. <strong>Today at 4:10 PM ET, they face the Padres again in a chance to reset and prove they can close out games when the pressure mounts.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 12, 2026"
