        "body": "The summer heat in Las Vegas just turned the spotlight on a rookie who might redefine the Raptors' ceiling. <strong>First-round pick Allen Graves exploded in his Summer League debut, posting 22 points, 13 rebounds, three steals, and two blocks</strong> despite an 83-80 overtime loss to Boston. After a 46-36 season that ended 70 days ago, Graves' dominance validates Bobby Webster's top pick and injects immediate hope into a roster still reshaping itself in draft and free agency. Graves, a versatile 6-foot-8 forward, didn't just show flashes; he commanded the floor, converting three of eight threes while controlling the paint. The front office now watches how this rookie foundation pairs with upcoming free-agent moves to close the gap atop the Atlantic Division. <strong>What to watch: Graves' next Summer League game and whether the Raptors use their cap space to add a veteran scorer before camp</strong>.",
